---

<section class="relative overflow-hidden py-10 mb-8">
  <div class="container mx-auto max-w-7xl px-4 relative z-10">
    <div class="flex flex-col md:flex-row gap-6 mb-6 justify-center">
      <div class="flex-1 min-w-[300px] rounded-lg border border-white/40 bg-white/65 p-6 shadow-lg backdrop-blur-sm">
        <h2 class="mb-2 text-2xl font-bold text-primary md:text-3xl">Who We Are</h2>
        <p class="text-left text-lg font-medium leading-relaxed text-gray-900">
          Religious Freedom Indiana (RFI) is a statewide coalition of Hoosiers
          who affirm that religious freedom is a right belonging to all, and
          that, in making and enforcing laws, government should not favor any
          interpretation based on one religious belief. RFI was founded in April
          2025 to educate about and to firmly but non-violently oppose
          Christian nationalism and other extremist beliefs that conflate
          religion and democracy.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="flex-1 min-w-[300px] rounded-lg border border-white/40 bg-white/65 p-6 shadow-lg backdrop-blur-sm">
        <h2 class="mb-2 text-2xl font-bold text-primary md:text-3xl">Where We're Headed</h2>
        <p class="text-left text-lg font-medium leading-relaxed text-gray-900">
          We envision a state and a nation governed by law without regard to
          religious beliefs, where every individual can freely worship, doubt,
          or disbelieve without facing fear, stigma, or coercion; where no
          government action favors one religion over others; and where all
          contribute to the common good.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="flex flex-col md:flex-row gap-6 mb-6 justify-center">
      <div class="flex-1 min-w-[300px] rounded-lg border border-white/40 bg-white/65 p-6 shadow-lg backdrop-blur-sm">
        <h2 class="mb-2 text-2xl font-bold text-primary md:text-3xl">Why We Exist</h2>
        <p class="text-left text-lg font-medium leading-relaxed text-gray-900">
          Movements advocating religious nationalism, whether Christian,
          Islamic, Jewish, or secular, weaponize faith to dominate other groups
          holding a different faith or no faith. Christian nationalism is
          particularly prevalent at the current time. This ideology distorts
          history, undermines democracy, and replaces persuasion with coercion.
        </p>
        <p class="mt-4 text-left text-lg font-medium leading-relaxed text-gray-900">
          We <b>oppose</b> statements that express ideas such as these:
        </p>
        <ul class="list-disc space-y-2 pl-6 text-left text-lg font-medium leading-relaxed text-gray-900">
          <li>The U.S. government should declare America a Christian nation.</li>
          <li>U.S. laws should be based on biblical Christian values.</li>
          <li>Being Christian is an important part of being truly American.</li>
          <li>God has called Christians to exercise dominion over all areas of American society.</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
      <div class="flex-1 min-w-[300px] rounded-lg border border-white/40 bg-white/65 p-6 shadow-lg backdrop-blur-sm">
        <h2 class="mb-2 text-2xl font-bold text-primary md:text-3xl">What We Do</h2>
        <ul class="list-disc space-y-2 pl-6 text-left text-lg font-medium leading-relaxed text-gray-900">
          <li>
            Educate the public with accurate, accessible resources about U.S.
            history and constitutional principles, especially separation of
            church and state.
          </li>
          <li>
            Expose and counter harmful disinformation, for example, myths of a
            "Christian nation," conspiracies about stolen elections, and
            slander of immigrants.
          </li>
          <li>Defend individuals and communities whose freedoms are under threat.</li>
          <li>
            Foster dialogue across beliefs, especially by engaging those who
            believe authoritarian Christian ideologies.
          </li>
          <li>
            Inspire action by training people to peacefully and effectively
            advocate in local governments, school boards, legislatures, and
            voting booths.
          </li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="mt-8 flex justify-center">
      <div class="w-full max-w-4xl rounded-lg border border-white/40 bg-white/70 p-6 shadow-lg backdrop-blur-sm">
        <h2 class="mb-4 text-left text-2xl font-bold text-primary md:text-center md:text-3xl">
          Our Core Values
        </h2>
        <div class="overflow-x-auto">
          <table class="min-w-full divide-y divide-blue-300 border border-blue-300 text-left">
            <thead class="bg-blue-50">
              <tr>
                <th class="px-4 py-3 text-lg font-bold text-primary">Principles</th>
                <th class="px-4 py-3 text-lg font-bold text-primary">Practices</th>
              </tr>
            </thead>
            <tbody class="divide-y divide-blue-200 bg-white/85">
              <tr>
                <td class="px-4 py-2 align-top font-medium leading-relaxed text-gray-900">Freedom</td>
                <td class="px-4 py-2 font-medium leading-relaxed text-gray-900">We persuade respectfully; we never impose beliefs.</td>
              </tr>
              <tr>
                <td class="px-4 py-2 align-top font-medium leading-relaxed text-gray-900">Humility</td>
                <td class="px-4 py-2 font-medium leading-relaxed text-gray-900">We stay teachable; absolute certainty fuels injustice.</td>
              </tr>
              <tr>
                <td class="px-4 py-2 align-top font-medium leading-relaxed text-gray-900">Truth</td>
                <td class="px-4 py-2 font-medium leading-relaxed text-gray-900">Evidence matters; ideology alone is insufficient.</td>
              </tr>
              <tr>
                <td class="px-4 py-2 align-top font-medium leading-relaxed text-gray-900">Pluralism</td>
                <td class="px-4 py-2 font-medium leading-relaxed text-gray-900">All people and identities welcomed.</td>
              </tr>
              <tr>
                <td class="px-4 py-2 align-top font-medium leading-relaxed text-gray-900">Non-partisanship</td>
                <td class="px-4 py-2 font-medium leading-relaxed text-gray-900">We encourage critique of policies and actions, not political parties.</td>
              </tr>
              <tr>
                <td class="px-4 py-2 align-top font-medium leading-relaxed text-gray-900">Non-violence</td>
                <td class="px-4 py-2 font-medium leading-relaxed text-gray-900">We encourage dialogue; we don't engage in threats, intimidation, and violence.</td>
              </tr>
            </tbody>
          </table>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
